In other words, sleep and introspection are part of what holds our own minds together. I bet this holds for machine minds, too.

Train for a bit. Let the proto-mind sleep and anneal the learning stress. Lather, rinse, repeat. And let it learn from questions asked, our reactions to the answers, and the answers themselves. Let it sleep and dream. Betcha it won't dream of electric sheep.
